e-only placement avoids that structural interaction and repeats the region analysis less often.\n\nThe final timing evidence is /tmp/zyntax-clif-fixes-late-controls on NUC and the corresponding -local directory locally. Fixed binaries, LLVM off, seven randomized process repetitions per mode, affinity 0-7; three seconds idle plus package \u003c=65 C before each sample; process/load/thermal monitoring and unchanged hashes. No Cargo/build commands between samples. Current native captures: /tmp/zyntax-clif-audit-combined-late on NUC and the corresponding -local directory. Measurements and the final commit SHA follow separately.\n\nFinal seven-process medians, baseline / candidate-with-region-reuse-disabled / normal candidate:\nPython nbody -n5 wall: 137.641 / 136.804 / 135.814 ms; mean kernel 7.567 / 7.439 / 7.271 ms.\nPython nbody -n50 wall: 336.862 / 330.346 / 321.217 ms; mean kernel 4.781 / 4.630 / 4.447 ms.\nPython FFT -n1 wall: 491.031 / 489.193 / 481.779 ms; kernel 301.782 / 299.185 / 294.467 ms.\nPython float -n5 wall: 101.164 / 100.667 / 100.626 ms.\nPython Richards -n5 wall: 127.756 / 129.092 / 128.919 ms. Its short kernel mean varied; the separate clean -n50 confirmation is wall 188.797 / 191.034 / 188.962 ms and mean 1.321 / 1.387 / 1.315 ms, so no sustained Richards regression is established.\nLua nbody wall: 205.086 / 207.722 / 206.983 ms; method_call: 119.644 / 121.498 / 120.525 ms; op_overload: 210.988 / 213.138 / 212.155 ms. Treat Lua as roughly flat, not improved.\n\nAll reported Python and method/operator cohorts have zero thermal counter increments. One final Lua nbody normal sample has a thermal flag and is retained. Desktop activity persisted; the shared lock and absence of build processes do not establish exclusive hardware isolation. Final and Richards sessions both report zero observed builds and matching executable hashes. The small early aggregate percentage remains provisional; use these final combined measurements for the accepted state.\n\nA